{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Moses implored.</b> One may say: this is the prayer referred to in the portion of Eikev — ״and I fell down before HaShem the forty days and the forty nights.״ After he descended and burned the calf and killed its worshippers — for reason cannot tolerate that he pray on their behalf until the idolaters among them were removed — and during those forty days He said to him, ״for I will not go up in your midst,״ and then Moses said to Him the entire passage ״see, You say to me,״ etc. And all those forty second days Moses did not ascend Mount Sinai, but rather prayed on their behalf in the tent he pitched for himself outside the camp, for how could he ascend to HaKadosh Barukh Hu without permission? And at their end, when HaKadosh Barukh Hu was appeased, He said to him, ״carve for yourself,״ etc., ״and you shall go up in the morning,״ etc. And he ascended Mount Sinai and stood there forty third days, and they concluded on the tenth of Tishrei." "<b>Why, HaShem, does Your anger burn against Your people?</b> Even though they did what they did, it is not for You to lose in one brief hour all the efforts and the good things You did for them. And further: why should the Egyptians say, etc. And further: what will You do regarding the oath to the fathers."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The reverent abbreviation הקב״ה is rendered as HaKadosh Barukh Hu per the directive to resolve abbreviations mechanically; however, this violates the rule that divine names must use the standard transliteration set."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:33.011803710Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}